# Check out every text file with LF line endings on all platforms (the
# repository already stores all text content as LF — verified with
# `git ls-files --eol`: 836 i/lf, 0 i/crlf).
#
# This is not cosmetic: `src-tauri/src/bin/monkey-cli/daemon/remote/web.rs`
# embeds the remote-controller UI assets at compile time via `include_str!`,
# so the served bytes of app.js/app.css/index.html are whatever line endings
# git happened to check out on the *build* machine. GitHub's Windows runners
# ship with `core.autocrlf=true`, which silently turned those assets (and
# every multi-line string test assertion about them) into CRLF on Windows
# builds only. Pinning eol=lf makes builds byte-identical across platforms.
#
# `text=auto` leaves binary files (git auto-detection) untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
